    "exception_flow": {
      "slot": "exception_flow",
      "claims": [
        {
          "content": "At a device-operation step during the closing sequence (e.g., Step 5), if an intermediate step results in a device control failure, the Operator with proper security can use Device Override to input the device status, overriding the status coming from the field, and continue the operating sequence through to the end (exit: continue the original closing sequence to completion).",
          "evidence_refs": [
            "EC-EF-007"
          ],
          "step_number": 5
        },
        {
          "content": "At a device-operation step during the closing sequence (e.g., Step 5), if a device fails to report completion of the current sequence step within the response time window allotted for the step, the closing sequence is halted. If the offending device status can be corrected within the configurable time period, the Operator can issue a resume command so the system attempts to complete the original closing sequence.",
          "evidence_refs": [
            "EC-EF-009",
            "EC-EF-023",
            "EC-EF-006",
            "EC-EF-024"
          ],
          "step_number": 5
        },
        {
          "content": "At any point in the closing sequence (e.g., at the Step 5 device-operation step), if the status of a closure device that was previously opened at the current entrance changes to 'unknown' or 'closed' without an operator-initiated command, the closing sequence is halted. If the offending device status can be corrected within the configurable time period, the Operator can issue a resume command so the system attempts to complete the original closing sequence.",
          "evidence_refs": [
            "EC-EF-016",
            "EC-EF-023",
            "EC-EF-006",
            "EC-EF-024"
          ],
          "step_number": 5
        },
        {
          "content": "During the closing sequence after a closure device has been closed (e.g., at the Step 6 device-operation step), if the status of that device at the current entrance changes to 'unknown' or 'open', the closing sequence is halted. If the offending device status can be corrected within the configurable time period, the Operator can issue a resume command so the system attempts to complete the original closing sequence.",
          "evidence_refs": [
            "EC-EF-022",
            "EC-EF-023",
            "EC-EF-006",
            "EC-EF-024"
          ],
          "step_number": 6
        },
        {
          "content": "At a device-operation step during the closing sequence (e.g., Step 5), if a device command must be issued outside the predetermined operational event, the Operator with proper security can use Operational Override to issue the device command on demand (exit: the on-demand device command is issued).",
          "evidence_refs": [
            "EC-EF-008"
          ],
          "step_number": 5
        }
      ],
      "evidence_card_ids": [
